-40. The owner-approved ODR-012 ruling, ADR-032, HC-096-03, and `[HASH-1]`–`[HASH-4]`
-    form one traceable contract: `Hash` remains in the prelude, `Hasher` and
-    `DefaultHasher` do not enter it, `finish` consumes the move-only context,
-    equal values hash equally, supplied spans do not escape, safe Map APIs expose
-    no mutable key, and no concrete mixing algorithm is frozen.
-41. ODR-013/ERR-054 are closed by the owner-selected generic
-    `fn hash[H: Hasher](self, mut h: H)` contract. `DefaultHasher implements Hasher`,
-    ordinary inference and monomorphization apply, and no bare-interface or
-    compiler-only dynamic conversion is inferred.
-42. The received post-H4 Revision 5 RFC remains byte-for-byte preserved at its recorded SHA-256,
-    ADR-034 records the owner's approval and later H5-materialization clarification, and H4 remains
-    byte-for-byte unchanged.
-43. One authoritative representation exists per semantic invariant; all indexes, caches, summaries,
-    serialization forms, backend forms, and `CallInfo`-style aggregates are derived and invalidated.
-44. `AccessContract`, `EffectSet`, initialization, provenance, retention, storage identity, access,
-    representation, ownership, checking, unsafe authority, synchronization, validity, and escape are
-    not collapsed by implementation grouping.
-45. Initialization retains `Uninit | Maybe | Init` plus required refinements, and absence of proof
-    grants no capability in every unknown-boundary domain.
-46. No `Len`/`Capacity` interface, duplicate collection abstraction, parallel safety system,
-    automatic dynamic-borrow fallback, or runtime capability metadata is introduced by H5.
-47. New feature work documents public/compiler/runtime complexity and reuses inference, generics,
-    interfaces, parameter modes, concrete APIs, metadata, and existing proof paths before adding a
-    programmer-visible concept.
-48. Primary diagnostics describe source semantics; compiler bookkeeping is secondary expert evidence.
-    View API documentation is generated from authoritative signatures/contracts where practical and
-    never becomes a hand-maintained semantic duplicate.
-49. Specification, implementation, owner-decision, and conformance ledgers remain separate, and no
-    implementation status is inferred merely from H6's requirements.
-50. The H4-to-H5 classified diff contains no source-language semantic, accepted-program,
-    rejected-program, observable-behavior, ABI, safety, effect, reload, or diagnostic-identity change.
-51. `[SPN-4]`–`[SPN-10]` define exactly four named public, non-prelude `@view` iterator/chunk types
-    under `std.collections`, use the existing associated-type `Iterator` interface, and introduce no
-    opaque-return or second ownership/lifetime mechanism.
-52. Shared and mutable iteration/chunking preserve ordinary reborrow, NLL, provenance, storage-
-    identity, and `[BRW-5]` disjointness semantics; zero-sized chunks panic through the existing
-    failure mechanism in every profile.
-53. `Span.as_ptr` and `MutSpan.as_ptr` return canonical Ember `*T`,
-    `MutSpan.as_mut_ptr` returns `*mut T`, extraction is safe, and pointer use and lifetime validity
-    remain governed by the existing unsafe rules without retaining or extending source storage.
-54. The preserved ODR-014 ruling, ADR-035, HC-096-06, `[SPN-4]`–`[SPN-10]`, and `[TST-25]` form one
-    traceable contract, while implementation and conformance remain unclaimed until executable
-    evidence exists.
